LICENCE AND SCOPE

Copyright (c) 2026 Albert Duncan. All rights reserved.

This repository holds the record of how a novel was made. It does not hold the
novel. Three kinds of material are in here and they are not covered by the same
terms. Read this before reusing anything.


1. THE RECORD AND THE SESSION LOGS -- all rights reserved

   The documents at the top level of this repository and everything in logs/:
   131 session transcripts in 138 files (128 distinct sessions), and the derived history, refusal record,
   claim and manifests built from them.

   No licence is granted. You may read them. You may not copy, redistribute,
   adapt, train machine learning models on, or publish them in whole or in part
   without the author's written permission.

   The logs quote the novel in places -- scattered single paragraphs, about 43
   per cent of its words in total, with the final chapter's prose removed. Those
   passages are part of the unpublished novel and no licence to them is granted
   by their appearing here.


2. THE TOOLING -- MIT

   The Python files in tools/: the builders for the history, the refusal record,
   the word-count snapshots and the session digest.

